  "html": "<p class=\"\">clipgoblin came out of a real editing problem. I was buried in a corpus of long recorded talks and lectures — hours of it — that I needed to actually navigate for a research project, and scrubbing Final Cut timelines to find the one moment someone said the thing was breaking me. So I built a tool that reads the transcript and drops a marker at every concept-relevant moment straight into the Final Cut timeline. Now I move through hours of footage by hitting <code class=\"md-inline-code\">Ctrl+'</code> instead of scrubbing.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"The CLI — generating concept-tagged FCPXML markers from a words.json transcript\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/clipgoblin/code2.png\" alt=\"The CLI — generating concept-tagged FCPXML markers from a words.json transcript\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/clipgoblin/code2.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/clipgoblin/code2.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/clipgoblin/code2.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/clipgoblin/code2.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"The CLI — generating concept-tagged FCPXML markers from a words.json transcript\" width=\"1400\" height=\"900\" style=\"--splay-rot:-1.52deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1400×900\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">The CLI — generating concept-tagged FCPXML markers from a words.json transcript</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"\">Under the hood it shells out to Whisper for word-level transcription, then generates concept-tagged FCPXML markers from the resulting <code class=\"md-inline-code\">words.json</code> — so each marker lands on the exact word, not a rough guess. It's the difference between an archive you dread opening and one you can move through at the speed of thought.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"Resolving and shelling out to whisper for word-level transcription\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/clipgoblin/code.png\" alt=\"Resolving and shelling out to whisper for word-level transcription\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/clipgoblin/code.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/clipgoblin/code.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/clipgoblin/code.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/clipgoblin/code.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"Resolving and shelling out to whisper for word-level transcription\" width=\"1400\" height=\"900\" style=\"--splay-rot:1.54deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1400×900\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">Resolving and shelling out to whisper for word-level transcription</figcaption>\n</figure>",
